ax cuts to people who are  not going to take the money they save  and use it to stimulate the economy so  really good reasons to be against this  tax cut are it's unethical it's immoral  and it's bad for the economy but it is  still 100  valid to point out that by the Wrights  own standards they should be against  this tax cut proposal because of the  deficit exploding effect that it's going  to have it's not a double standard by  the left its accurately pointing out the  double standard from the right okay so  prepare for that red herring that you're  going to hear from the talking heads and  the pundits and everybody else it's  almost boring and passe though right  there's nothing shocking about tax cuts  for the rich blowing up the deficit the  george w bush tax cuts for the rich did  the exact same thing this is just what  happens when you cut taxes for the rich  this is why the simplistic talking  points around taxes from the right are  so destructive and we'll be having some  debates on the program about taxation  sooner than later they create these  simple narratives they take a really  complex issue like taxation and they  reduce it to hey taxes are bad because  it's your money you should keep your  money because it's yours eliminate as  many taxes as possible okay but hold on  a second you don't want to pay taxes and  you don't want to increase the debt but  you also want a stronger and stronger  meaning bigger and bigger military but  you don't want to pay taxes and you  don't want to increase the debt on and  on in this dumb vicious circle so it  doesn't make any sense and along these  lines i want to prepare you for another  talking point that you're going to hear  which originated with trump trump has  said and he might say again that the  scoring by the CBO doesn't take into  account all of the increased revenue for  the government from the new wages and  production of stuff and hiring of people  because these tax cuts will cause growth  do not fall for it there is no evidence  whatsoever period that they can point to  it has never worked that way it will not  work that way no serious economic  analysis tells us that the tax cuts are  going to generate such significant new  government revenue that it's all going  to work out - even in the end it's not  going to happen okay and while we're at  it added one other thing  that is sort of starting to circulate  there are some right-wingers tweeting  posting online that this is better than  Obama because Obama added nine trillion  to the debt over eight years and that  this is only 1.7 trillion over ten years  so it's not quite as bad this 1.7  trillion that's going to be added to the  debt over 10 years that's just the  impact of this tax bill right  it doesn't include everything else  that's going on that will add to the  deficit remember Obama reduced the  deficit but it was still positive so the  debt went up not as quickly as before  but it still went up because we were  running a deficit a smaller deficit and  of course the debt is the sum total of  Prior deficits or surpluses that have  been run Republicans are somewhere in  the in the neighborhood of adding 1.2  trillion to the deficit already running  a 1.2 trillion dollar deficit already  this would per year this will add to  that so don't be tricked by that okay be  prepared for the talking points and  we'll definitely be following the path  of this totally abortive tax plan  through committee for you and will  report on if and when it will pass the  video you just finished watching was  made possible by you through the  membership program you can sign up for  membership at david pakman.com slash  membership we are viewer supported  independent media you can use the coupon  code  I voted 17 for a 40% discount off of  your membership
 

